                  "tools/actuals-record-validator/main_test.go:552-578"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 9 changed paths in the supplied patches.",
              "The validator change from `*claimed != counted.Lenses \u0026\u0026 counted.Results == 0` to `counted.Results == 0` is sound: the task log states a stored result always records at least one row, so Results==0 implies Lenses==0, and the later case still handles a mismatch when results exist. The refusal path is covered for an empty repo and for a repo holding only another change's results.",
              "The CI guard compares the basename of each record to the legacy fixture, so every other record is validated as written. This closes the earlier jq-bypass warning. The test pins the guard, the single jq deletion and the instance variable.",
              "A new test shows a semantic refusal (exit 6) is returned before an unreadable --repo (exit 7), which proves the documented ordering.",
              "TestAPassPrintsTwoLinesAndTheUsageTextSaysSo checks that a pass prints two lines and that the usage text says so, so the change in output shape is observable and documented. saysOK uses the schema path, so refusal tests cannot pass vacuously on the usage text.",
